{
  "_doc": "THE single source of truth for model selection — read by Python (bob_models.py). Converted from the retired config/models.psd1; full field prose is in that file's git history. Per-model schema: repo/path=HuggingFace repo+file -> download URL; gguf=local filename in models/ (also the -m runtime path); ctx=context window (-c). ALWAYS set it, embedders and rerankers included: with no -c llama-server reserves the model's full trained window, which measured 4.8 GB for the 0.6B embedder and 5.7 GB for the 0.6B reranker versus 1.4 GB each at -c 2048; sizeGB=approx on-disk size; kv=true applies the KV-cache quant macro; flags=extra llama-server flags (appended last, so they override srv-macro defaults); ngl=\"auto\" drops -ngl so llama.cpp fits the offload to free VRAM itself (needed for a DENSE model bigger than the card, where --n-cpu-moe does not apply); setParams=server-side sampling enforcement; kvQuantK/kvQuantV override the profile-wide KV quant for one model (a long-context model held entirely in VRAM can only afford q4_0); aliasOf=\"<role>\" makes this role a second NAME for that model rather than a second model — it inherits the target's whole spec, downloads once, loads once, and is emitted under llama-swap `aliases:` with its own setParams routed through setParamsByID; ttl=0 never auto-unloads; pinned=true keeps resident (excluded from the swap group); embedding adds --embedding. Keys starting with '_' are METADATA (e.g. _targetVRAM, _notes, _cpuTier), not models — skipped by the generator and downloader. activeProfile here is the shipped DEFAULT; the writable override lives in data/active-profile.json (bob profile) and env BOB_PROFILE wins for one invocation. Tunable knobs (defaults block) are overridable per-machine in config/user.json (deep-merged). Re-run `bob gen` after editing.",
  "activeProfile": "16gb",
  "defaults": {
    "mlockBig": false,
    "kvQuantK": "q8_0",
    "ubatch": 512,
    "flashAttn": true,
    "langfuseEnabled": false,
