      "_notes": "One Qwen3.8-27B GSQ-RCO IQ3_XXS (10.09 GB) serves chat/coder/ponder/writer/agent, fully on the card: no expert offload, no dense spill. MEASURED on a 16 GB RTX 5080 with a running desktop — chat 10950 MiB at 40960 ctx / q4_0 KV, embed 1198, rerank 1198, so Bob holds 13.3 GB and leaves ~0.9 GB beside a ~2 GB compositor. Three things buy that: -c on the 0.6B helpers (with none they reserve their full 32K window — 4.8 GB and 5.7 GB), -ub 128 on the same two (~226 MiB each), and -np 1 (llama-server defaults to four slots, each with its own KV and, on this hybrid attention/SSM model, its own recurrent-state cache). fim joins the swap group here: a resident FIM model does not fit next to a 10 GB chat model, so IDE autocomplete and chat take turns. The -mtp build of the same model is the speed profile (+40% tok/s) but costs ~900 MiB more, which this tier does not have."
